id: pm-rlm-b8cs
title: Adaptive decomposition with declared budgets
description: "Compare bounded execution-time decomposition strategies from caller-declared question parts and remaining budget. Reuse certified RLM reads, settings, reservations, evidence contracts and durable terminal call records; no training or promotion."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T14:30:16.189Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T14:48:15.465Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Tiny budgets produce typed partial answers; Child failures preserve terminal evidence; Strategy comparisons are deterministic under scripted fixtures
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T14:31:03.211Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against CLI 2026.10.23 and current package sources/docs: pm-rlm recursion follows model actions; pm-rl learns and promotes policies; pm-context packs context under token ceilings; pm-swarm schedules work and resources. No bounded planner comparing caller-declared question decompositions was found. This feature will compare whole/pairs/components deterministically without inference during planning, execute only the selected plan using native RLM runs, preserve each child terminal ledger, and return typed partial components and stop reasons. No training or promotion. The pinned SDK remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T14:39:48.308Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses the pinned SDK for certified full reads, schema fields, item creation/claims/comments/closure, and native RLM run reservations, settlement, witnessed answers and terminal evidence. Three fixed candidates compare exact first-step admission with stable tie-breaking; only the selected candidate executes. One source snapshot is frozen across children. Public read-only validation: 12 items, 54941 JSON bytes, 30 files unchanged; 3 strategies, 3 supported parts, 3 logical children, 6 fixture steps, 3 successful read-only replays; charge 24481, remainder 275519, receipt 1283 bytes. One-token run: zero calls and 3 deferred parts. Forced failure: 1 closed terminal child. No git executable during execution and no external inference. See docs/adaptive-validation.json."
  "2026-10-23T14:43:04.120Z",codex-agent,"Targeted SDK and CLI acceptance includes native TOON/JSON dispatch without git, zero/tiny budget partials, deterministic strategy receipts, supported and unknown components, shared accounting, call/context ceilings, malformed declarations with remedies, nested terminal failures and persistence refusal. The existing RLM engine was factored only to share exact initial reservation calculation and native run preparation. Controller interruption is explicitly documented: inspect checkpoints and native child runs; no automatic controller resume or retry."
  "2026-10-23T14:47:03.792Z",codex-agent,"Local evidence: 12 adaptive cases passed across the 11-case linked run plus the adapter-boundary regression; 7 existing engine/command cases passed. Targeted coverage of src/adaptive.ts is 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. node test/adaptive-revert.ts passed 3/3 proofs: each acceptance regression fails with only its corresponding implementation behavior reverted, and exact source bytes are restored. Linked public validation passed again; all source bytes unchanged. Typecheck, lint, docstrings, duplication (0%) and identity checks pass. Full unchanged release gates are delegated to CI npm and Bun, not run on the saturated local host. PM linked-test result tracking is disabled in this tracker, so results are recorded in these comments instead of changing tracker policy. Controller resume is an explicit documented limitation; child ledgers retain native replay/recovery."
  "2026-10-23T14:48:15.465Z",codex-agent,"Strict tracker health passed with an isolated home and system/global git configuration disabled, matching clean CI identity. The ordinary local invocation detects a globally installed pm-github host-version skew; that external runtime is outside this change. No tracker history was rewritten. The item remains in_progress and released for orchestrator verification; no merge or release is authorized."
